# HDL

1. Document Q-format in `docs/fixed_point_notes.md` **before** writing RTL.
2. Write the testbench **first**. Stop. Do not write the DUT until the human has reviewed the TB.
3. Compare against **checked-in fixture vectors** from Phase 2 (under the fixtures path documented in PLAN.md / Phase 2 acceptance), not a prose description of expected behavior.
4. A testbench the same agent also wrote is not trusted alone — human review of TB logic (reset, clocks, stimulus, compare window) is required before RTL.
5. Synthesis / timing / hardware reports are human-run checkpoints. Author TCL only; never invent report contents or claim success without pasted logs.
